   "definition_quote": "An instance of the \\QFK problem is of the form $(\\A, n, m, k, \\epsilon, \\delta)$, where $\\A$ is a set of arms with $|\\A| = n \\geq 2$; $m \\in \\{1, 2, \\dots, n - 1\\}$; $k \\in \\{1, \\dots, m\\}$; tolerance $\\epsilon \\in (0, 1]$; and mistake probability $\\delta \\in (0,1]$. An algorithm $\\mathcal{L}$ is said to solve\n\\QFK if for every instance of \\QFK, it terminates\nwith probability 1, and returns $k$ \\emph{distinct} $(\\epsilon, m)$-optimal arms with probability at least $1-\\delta$."
